{"id":"158986a9-7d0e-4737-9684-3d400d339b8e","revision":0,"last_node_id":31,"last_link_id":8,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,0],"size":[340,330],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Read me","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"MarkdownNote","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["## DLSS5 Video Upscaler\n\n**1.** Switch features on or off in the **Control Panel** below.\n\n**2.** In **1 · Input**, pick your video - or set the panel to *Batch folder* and choose a folder.\n\n**3.** Steps **2-4** are already set to the measured best. Change them only if you want to.\n\n**4.** Press **Run**. The result appears in **5 · Render**.\n\n*Greyed-out nodes and settings are switched off and are skipped.*\n*Tip: **Quick preview** renders the first 5 seconds so you can check the look first.*\n\n---\nNeeds: ComfyUI-DLSS5-Enhancer (+ its runtime), ComfyUI Nvidia VFX Nodes, ComfyUI-Frame-Interpolation (RIFE 4.9), ComfyUI-DLSS5-VideoHelpers - and an RTX 30/40/50 GPU."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## DLSS5 Video Upscaler\n\n**1.** Switch features on or off in the **Control Panel** below.\n\n**2.** In **1 · Input**, pick your video - or set the panel to *Batch folder* and choose a folder.\n\n**3.** Steps **2-4** are already set to the measured best. Change them only if you want to.\n\n**4.** Press **Run**. The result appears in **5 · Render**.\n\n*Greyed-out nodes and settings are switched off and are skipped.*\n*Tip: **Quick preview** renders the first 5 seconds so you can check the look first.*\n\n---\nNeeds: ComfyUI-DLSS5-Enhancer (+ its runtime), ComfyUI Nvidia VFX Nodes, ComfyUI-Frame-Interpolation (RIFE 4.9), ComfyUI-DLSS5-VideoHelpers - and an RTX 30/40/50 GPU."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"DLSS5ControlPanel","pos":[0,380],"size":[340,178],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"Mode","name":"batch_folder","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"batch_folder"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"RTX deblur","name":"rtx_deblur","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"rtx_deblur"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"60 FPS","name":"fps_60","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"fps_60"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"30 FPS","name":"fps_30","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"fps_30"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"HDR output","name":"hdr","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"hdr"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"Quick preview (5 s)","name":"quick_preview","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"quick_preview"},"link":null}],"outputs":[],"title":"Control Panel","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"DLSS5ControlPanel","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":[true,true,true,false,false,false],"widgets_values_named":{"batch_folder":true,"rtx_deblur":true,"fps_60":true,"fps_30":false,"hdr":false,"quick_preview":false},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":3,"type":"Note","pos":[-556.9722708874782,-49.03789460303798],"size":[520,560],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Details & measurements","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"Note","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["DETAILS & MEASUREMENTS (RTX 5090)\n\nORDER: 2a RTX deblur (source res) -> 2b RIFE 60 fps -> 2c optional RTX pre-upscale -> 3 DLSS5 -> 4 RTX HDR. Steps 2a-2c run as one pass into one near-lossless temp file. Nothing is ever loaded into RAM, so 10-minute videos are fine.\n\nWHY (LPIPS vs ground truth on degraded clips + crops of real MiniMax footage):\n- RTX passes after DLSS5 never helped; deblur before it did - DLSS5 rebuilds more skin/hair/edge detail from sharper input.\n- DEBLUR_ULTRA @ 0.5 = best all-rounder (0.059 vs DLSS5 alone 0.063 light compression; 0.096 vs 0.104 heavy). 1.0 looks painted.\n- DENOISE before DLSS5 was worse in every test; STREAMING_ULTRA too.\n- 3x total: rtx_pre_upscale 1.5x + DLSS5 2x beat DLSS5 3x (0.088 vs 0.098).\n- HDR must be last (DLSS5 is 8-bit SDR). RTX Frame Generation only does whole multiples (24 -> 48), so RIFE does 60.\n\nSPEED, 20 s of 1080p30 -> 4K: DLSS5 43 s | + deblur 61 s | + 60 fps 121 s | + HDR 203 s (per 10 min of 30 fps: ~22 / 31 / 60 / 100 min).\n\nTIPS\n- 60 FPS / 30 FPS (only one at a time): clips already at or above the target are left alone (30 FPS never slows a 60 fps clip down); hard cuts are held, not morphed. 24 -> 30 adds 25% more frames for DLSS5.\n- HDR: HLG looks fine on normal screens too; PQ (HDR10) is for HDR TVs/monitors. keep_sdr also saves the SDR file.\n- Edited videos with many cuts: set DLSS5 > scene_change_threshold (advanced) to ~0.10.\n- Output cap 7680x4320 (final size = rtx_pre_upscale x DLSS5 mode). Quality 'Max' measured worse than 'Good'.\n- Batch: finished clips are skipped (resume), broken ones are reported; results are <name>_DLSS5.<ext>.\n- Don't run another GPU job at the same time."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"DETAILS & MEASUREMENTS (RTX 5090)\n\nORDER: 2a RTX deblur (source res) -> 2b RIFE 60 fps -> 2c optional RTX pre-upscale -> 3 DLSS5 -> 4 RTX HDR. Steps 2a-2c run as one pass into one near-lossless temp file. Nothing is ever loaded into RAM, so 10-minute videos are fine.\n\nWHY (LPIPS vs ground truth on degraded clips + crops of real MiniMax footage):\n- RTX passes after DLSS5 never helped; deblur before it did - DLSS5 rebuilds more skin/hair/edge detail from sharper input.\n- DEBLUR_ULTRA @ 0.5 = best all-rounder (0.059 vs DLSS5 alone 0.063 light compression; 0.096 vs 0.104 heavy). 1.0 looks painted.\n- DENOISE before DLSS5 was worse in every test; STREAMING_ULTRA too.\n- 3x total: rtx_pre_upscale 1.5x + DLSS5 2x beat DLSS5 3x (0.088 vs 0.098).\n- HDR must be last (DLSS5 is 8-bit SDR). RTX Frame Generation only does whole multiples (24 -> 48), so RIFE does 60.\n\nSPEED, 20 s of 1080p30 -> 4K: DLSS5 43 s | + deblur 61 s | + 60 fps 121 s | + HDR 203 s (per 10 min of 30 fps: ~22 / 31 / 60 / 100 min).\n\nTIPS\n- 60 FPS / 30 FPS (only one at a time): clips already at or above the target are left alone (30 FPS never slows a 60 fps clip down); hard cuts are held, not morphed. 24 -> 30 adds 25% more frames for DLSS5.\n- HDR: HLG looks fine on normal screens too; PQ (HDR10) is for HDR TVs/monitors. keep_sdr also saves the SDR file.\n- Edited videos with many cuts: set DLSS5 > scene_change_threshold (advanced) to ~0.10.\n- Output cap 7680x4320 (final size = rtx_pre_upscale x DLSS5 mode). Quality 'Max' measured worse than 'Good'.\n- Batch: finished clips are skipped (resume), broken ones are reported; results are <name>_DLSS5.<ext>.\n- Don't run another GPU job at the same time."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":10,"type":"LoadVideo","pos":[440,0],"size":[320,629.2941176470588],"flags":{},"order":3,"mode":2,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"file","name":"file","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"file"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"choose file to upload","name":"upload","type":"IMAGEUPLOAD","widget":{"name":"upload"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"VIDEO","name":"VIDEO","type":"VIDEO","links":[1]}],"title":"Video","properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.42.1","Node name for S&R":"LoadVideo","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["","image"],"widgets_values_named":{"file":"","upload":"image"},"color":"#2a363b","bgcolor":"#3f5159"},{"id":11,"type":"DLSS5BatchFolderInput","pos":[445.1834153356637,729.6297948713847],"size":[320,58],"flags":{},"order":4,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"Input folder","name":"input_folder","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"input_folder"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"folder","name":"folder","type":"DLSS5_FOLDER","links":[2]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"DLSS5BatchFolderInput","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_value